  1044                              <1> ; waitk. At a console: a wait on the input handle for the time (EAX: 0
  1045                              <1> ; just looks, -1 is INFINITE), then ReadConsoleInputA for one event. The
  1046                              <1> ; wait is WaitForMultipleObjects, on v_hin alone or on v_hin and v_htm,
  1047                              <1> ; which follow each other. A timed wait (1 ms or more) sets the
  1048                              <1> ; high-resolution timer once for the whole time and waits for the input or
  1049                              <1> ; the timer, with no time of its own; without the timer it is a plain wait
  1050                              <1> ; on the input for the time, which starts again with its whole time after
  1051                              <1> ; each event passed over. Only key-down events count: their character,
  1052                              <1> ; or for the left and right arrow keys (virtual keys 25h and 27h, which
  1053                              <1> ; have none) ^B and ^F. Anything else is passed over.
  1054                              <1> ; Input that is not a console (a pipe or a file) is read a byte at a time
  1055                              <1> ; with ReadFile, and only by a wait that is not just a look (a look would
  1056                              <1> ; eat the input); at its end the interpreter exits.
